From 8342d1f694258f9b660a1246bb1ba52f658ec377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:57:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-87: Ctrl+drag = a copy dropped there, like
 WinForms / WPF (0.87.0)

WinForms / WPF designers: holding Ctrl while dragging a component copies it;
the copy lands where it is let go and the original stays. Here Ctrl+drag was a
plain move (Ctrl only toggled the selection). Now a Ctrl press on a component
starts a copy drag of the selection (one not selected joins first, as the
click would); on the release the originals go back where they were and the
probe posts copyDrop (names, dx, dy) -- no style edit. The extension
(cmdCopyDrop) puts each copy right after its original (same container, drawn
over it), new names (spbSave -> spbSave_2), moved by dx / dy, the first copy
selected, ONE undo. Ctrl+click without a move still adds / takes out of the
selection. A lock does not stop a copy (the original does not move).

README / CHEATSHEET: Ctrl+drag; the safety note no longer says Ctrl+click
passes clicks to the page (it has not for a long time). WPF_DIFF_LOG.md: item 8
done, 0.86 commit filled in, new open items 11-14 from the XAML Designer pages
(outline Ctrl+H / Ctrl+L, artboard background, zoom 12.5-800 %, reset one
layout property).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 176, panels, real VS Code 152): probe
(Ctrl+drag 20,10 -> copyDrop with both names, no edit, the originals back;
Ctrl+click on a selected one takes it out, no copy); smoke (two copied, each
right after its original, +30 / -12; no move / unknown name = nothing; the
message route); real VS Code (spbSave_2 40 px right, drawn in Panel2 and
selected, spbSave where it was; one undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
